1) Git - is a version controlling system r source code management 
  vcs means which accepts the code coming from all the sources & integrating the code to make it as a single project 
vcs is of 2 types centralised vcs and distributed vcs (GIT) , it can work offline

2) GITHUB - is an open source version controlling platform for managing git repositories and collaboration among teams,
  by providing collaborative platform with features like pm,issue tracking, code reviews & enhancing team collaboration.

3) Git clone - clone means carbon copy
  git clone is used to download the entire code from the git hub r remote repository to local repository
  mostly used once

4) Git pull - pull command downloads only the updated code from the rr to lr
  used multiple times 
  this command downloads the code directly on the current working branch

5) Git fetch - fetch command downloads only the updated code from rr into a separate branch of lr
  this provides a chance to verify the downloaded code, later it can be merged with the required branch

6) git remote - is  a connection to a git repository that is stored somewhere usually like github,gitlab
    git remote -v

7) origin - is simply a  name (alias) for a remote git repository

8) working directory - where the code gets created ,files r called untracked files
   staging area - the files r code get implemented by version controlling, files r called indexed files
   local repository - place where the files get preserved r pushed into rr , files r called committed files

9) git push - when the git push command is used the local commits get uploaded into the rr r github
     
